      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is something we've been dying for in Australia & NZ. Sure server costs are expensive here, and bandwidth might be an initial issue, but truthfully as someone who does pay for VRC+, I'm a bit disappointed that there's still no clear direction for us in down-under-land. We're forgotten about constantly, and we're still a large enough community to be recognised!\n\nWe have our own subcommunities and host events on VRC, but having US-West the best (and most stable compared to JP) servers as the only viable option is laughable. We all live in the same country, yet we aren't even able to talk without 200+ms ping. It'd be bloody nice to have a convo with a fellow Aussie/Kiwi without accidentally talking over one another.\n\nVote this please!~",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
